// End-to-end example for task 4168 (geom-transform ε): `arbitrary_pattern`'s
// LIST form — a `List<Transform<3>>` carrying a full per-instance rigid
// transform (rotation + translation) — additively alongside the existing
// scalar-triple (translation-only) form exercised by
// examples/pattern_composition.ri's `PatternComposed.shifted`. Supersedes the
// phantom-partial task 323 (translation-only arbitrary_pattern).
//
// Running
//
//     reify eval examples/pattern_arbitrary_transforms.ri
//
// unions `box(2mm, 2mm, 10mm)` with a single copy rotated 90° about the Y
// axis (zero translation) via the LIST form, and surfaces the resulting
// geometry's mass through the `Physical` spec-shape trait (mirrors
// examples/spec-shape-physical.ri):
//
//   ArbitraryTransformBracket.mass = volume(geometry) * material.density
//
// A 90°-about-Y rotation swaps the box's X and Z extents (2mm <-> 10mm), so
// the union of the original box (X:[-1,1] Y:[-1,1] Z:[-5,5] mm) with its
// rotated copy (X:[-5,5] Y:[-1,1] Z:[-1,1] mm) has volume
// 40 + 40 - 8 = 72 mm^3 (their 2x2x2mm cube intersection is subtracted once)
// — observably different from either box alone. This is the signal that the
// per-instance rotation is honored end-to-end (compiler list-form lowering
// -> eval decode -> IR per-instance transforms -> kernel rigid transform)
// rather than silently dropped (task 323's translation-only regression,
// which would instead yield the un-rotated box's volume of 40 mm^3).
structure def ArbitraryTransformBracket : Physical {
    param geometry : Solid = arbitrary_pattern(
        box(2mm, 2mm, 10mm),
        [transform3(orient_axis_angle(vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), 90deg), vec3(0mm, 0mm, 0mm))]
    )
    param material : Material = Material(
        name: "Steel AISI 1045",
        density: 7850kg/m^3,
        youngs_modulus: 205GPa
    )
}
